    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"assets/images/threadline-cover.png\" alt=\"Threadline 2.0: file relation map on the left, two columns of directory cards on the right, turn status and hover linking\" width=\"100%\">\n</p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "<h1 align=\"center\">Threadline · 脉络</h1>\n<p align=\"center\">A permanent read-only visual map of how a DeepSeek Harness workspace actually developed.</p>\n<p align=\"center\"><a href=\"README.zh.md\">中文</a></p>\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://www.typescriptlang.org/\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/TypeScript-5.x-3178C6?logo=typescript&logoColor=white\" alt=\"TypeScript\"></a>\n  <a href=\"https://react.dev/\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/React-18-61DAFB?logo=react&logoColor=white\" alt=\"React 18\"></a>\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/DeepSeek%20Harness-plugin-4B6BFB\" alt=\"DeepSeek Harness plugin\"></a>\n  <a href=\"LICENSE\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-green\" alt=\"License MIT\"></a>\n  <a href=\"CHANGELOG.md\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/version-1.0.0-blue\" alt=\"Version 1.0.0\"></a>\n</p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Overview",
      "text": "Threadline answers a question that chat logs do not: **what did this workspace actually go through, and what did each turn change?**\n\nIt reads what DeepSeek Harness has already recorded — sessions, subagents, tool calls, file operations, commands, background jobs — and turns it into a growing relationship map of the current workspace. Files that DSH touched become nodes, grouped by directory; turns become a strip at the bottom; every number can be traced back to a recorded event."
    },
    {
      "section": "Overview",
      "text": "It is **permanently read-only**. It never writes to your workspace, your session logs or your settings, never calls a model, and never makes an outbound request. It cannot start, stop or retry anything — there is deliberately no control surface at all.\n\nTypical use: you come back to a long session, or hand a workspace to someone else, and want to see where the work went."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- **File relation map (left)** — the most active directory of the current session by default. Pick any directory card to switch; pick a turn to switch to the files touched by that turn across directories. Deterministic radial layout, no pan/zoom, no cluster boxes, no grid. Node colour = five file families (text / code / data / media / other).\n- **Directory cards (right, two columns)** — name, file count, current-turn badge, operations / last activity, five-family bar, top 3 active files. Same screen as the map, one page scroll; stacks below 960px.\n- **Turn status only from recorded facts** — `read N`, `write +A / −D lines`, `first seen`; file-level deletion/creation is not provable and is not shown. The summary bar is fixed to one line: `read N · write +A/−D lines · first seen F · deletes C` (full wording in the tooltip).\n- **Two-way hover linking** — hover a card to preview its directory; hover a node to highlight its directory card and related turns; hover a turn to preview that turn's files and highlight related cards. Hover only previews; it never changes the click selection or scroll position.\n- **Per-turn impact icon** — under a finished assistant message; click jumps to the "
    },
    {
      "section": "Installation",
      "text": "Requirements: DeepSeek Harness **0.2.2-rc.1** or newer, on a desktop or web profile.\n\nInstall it as a DSH plugin from npm:\n\n```text\nPlugin manager → Add plugin → dsh-plugin-control-your-development@1.0.0\n```\n\nOr install into a profile directly:\n\n```bash\ndsh plugin add dsh-plugin-control-your-development@1.0.0 --profile desktop\n```\n\nThen reload the page (client code) or restart DSH (host code)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Installation",
      "text": "> Installed DSH plugins do not update automatically. Upgrading means uninstalling and installing the new version — this is a DSH behaviour, not a Threadline one."
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "Open a conversation and pick the **Threadline** tab next to chat / trajectory. The tab fills the conversation area and scrolls on its own; the composer is hidden while you are in it and returns when you leave.\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"assets/images/threadline-map.png\" alt=\"Threadline 2.0: file relation map on the left, two directory card columns on the right, one page scroll\" width=\"100%\">\n</p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "- The left map shows the current directory; pick another directory card to switch, or a turn block to switch to that turn's file map with status.\n- Hovering a card, node or turn previews and cross-highlights; clicking pins the selection; leaving the whole tab restores it.\n- The timeline plays the workspace back in time; ranges are **today / 7 days / 30 days / all**.\n- `/threadline` jumps to the tab; the per-turn impact icon jumps and focuses that turn."
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"assets/images/threadline-turn.png\" alt=\"Turn view: read / written-line / first-seen status and delete-command count\" width=\"100%\">\n</p>\n\nThreadline only reads the workspace the current session belongs to. Sessions from other workspaces, profiles or machines are not aggregated."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "None. There is no configuration file, no setting, no stored preference and no cached artefact — all filters, selections and time ranges live in memory and reset when you reload. The only thing it needs is the workspace it is already in."
    },
    {
      "section": "Project structure",
      "text": "```text\nplugin/\n  src/shared/      event reducer, relation engine, reference parsers\n  src/host/        read-only scan, in-memory index, local read-only routes\n  src/client/      data layer, UI, three entries"
    },
    {
      "section": "Releases",
      "text": "Current release: **panel plugin v1.0.0** (stable).\n\nSee [CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md) for what changed in each version, and the [Releases](https://github.com/HaoyanZhang123/dsh-plugin-control-your-development/releases) page for installable versions."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "[MIT](LICENSE)"
    }
